1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,753
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,837 --> 00:00:07,757
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,341 --> 00:00:10,677
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,429
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,512 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,268
[Tonet] <i>Ibyang is at my brother's shop.</i>

7
00:00:18,351 --> 00:00:20,645
<i>She's still crying.</i>

8
00:00:20,729 --> 00:00:23,523
She just stopped your bratty daughter!

9
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:26,401
Hey, hey. Don't talk about
my child like that.

10
00:00:26,484 --> 00:00:28,820
[Tonet] <i>If you don't want the kid, say so!</i>

11
00:00:28,903 --> 00:00:31,614
<i>Don't make her feel worthless!</i>

12
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:32,824
[Atoy] Tomorrow,

13
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:34,659
I'll take you both out!

14
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:36,244
Where are we going?

15
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:37,954
Why did you even come back?

16
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:40,165
[Janine] <i>You're not the real child.</i>

17
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:41,291
[Tonet] <i>Honestly,</i>

18
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:44,043
<i>her attitude is really different</i>
<i>from you and Atoy.</i>

19
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:47,380
[Audrey] But even so,
Janine is my flesh and blood.

20
00:00:47,464 --> 00:00:51,426
Uh, speaking of blood, there's…

21
00:00:51,509 --> 00:00:53,428
There's a donation drive at the court now.

22
00:00:53,511 --> 00:00:54,554
What's your blood type?

23
00:00:54,637 --> 00:00:55,722
[in English] O positive.

24
00:00:55,805 --> 00:00:56,765
- [teenager] <i>Brother, brother!</i>
- [Atoy] <i>Oh?</i>

25
00:00:56,848 --> 00:00:57,682
[teenager] <i>Can I take a picture of you?</i>

26
00:00:57,766 --> 00:00:58,975
<i>You look so cute as father and child.</i>

27
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:00,393
You even look alike.

28
00:01:00,477 --> 00:01:02,520
I'm his real daughter, not her.

29
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:06,024
[Tonet] <i>The mother and father</i>
<i>are both O positive.</i>

30
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:09,652
But their child is AB positive.

31
00:01:09,736 --> 00:01:10,904
Is that possible?

32
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:13,364
No. It's impossible.

33
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:15,617
So, Janine isn't Atoy's child?

34
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,744
[Martina] Isn't it unsettling that Atoy

35
00:01:17,827 --> 00:01:19,287
has been with Janine for that long?

36
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:22,332
What if he notices or finds out
she isn't his child?

37
00:01:22,415 --> 00:01:25,460
I need to talk to Atoy now. Wait.

38
00:01:25,543 --> 00:01:26,586
Ah?

39
00:01:26,669 --> 00:01:28,421
PREVIOUSLY

40
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:29,756
Atoy?

41
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:32,050
Ibyang!

42
00:01:32,133 --> 00:01:34,302
[ominous music playing]

43
00:01:34,385 --> 00:01:35,553
Atoy!

44
00:01:38,389 --> 00:01:39,599
Ibyang!

45
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:44,229
Oh, miss! Miss?

46
00:01:44,312 --> 00:01:45,897
Did you see a man?

47
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:48,775
He's tall, really handsome,

48
00:01:48,858 --> 00:01:51,444
and he was with two little girls.

49
00:01:51,528 --> 00:01:52,862
Ah, yes, earlier.

50
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:55,615
They were playing hopscotch there.

51
00:01:55,698 --> 00:01:56,658
They already left.

52
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:58,493
Ah, where did they go?

53
00:01:58,576 --> 00:01:59,786
I don't know.

54
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:01,496
[music fades]

55
00:02:01,579 --> 00:02:02,747
[in English] Thank you.

56
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:05,917
[sauve theme music playing]

57
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,335
[motorcycle revving]

58
00:02:07,418 --> 00:02:08,294
[sewing machine whirring]

59
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:09,254
[scratches]

60
00:02:09,337 --> 00:02:11,256
[snipping]

61
00:02:11,881 --> 00:02:13,716
[sewing machine clacking]

62
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:17,303
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

63
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:18,513
[thumps and gunshots]

64
00:02:18,596 --> 00:02:20,807
[clacking]

65
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:22,892
[snipping]

66
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:28,857
[electronic blipping]

67
00:02:31,568 --> 00:02:34,737
[muffled chattering]

68
00:02:37,657 --> 00:02:38,658
It's Gavin.

69
00:02:44,998 --> 00:02:46,082
[Karla] Gavin.

70
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:48,334
How was your date with Cathy?

71
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:49,669
You're not telling me anything.

72
00:02:50,587 --> 00:02:52,338
Looks like it won't work out.

73
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:53,798
Did she reject you?

74
00:02:55,216 --> 00:02:58,136
[melancholic music playing]

75
00:02:58,219 --> 00:03:00,597
You know what? That's okay.

76
00:03:01,764 --> 00:03:04,559
You'll find a girl who's really for you.

77
00:03:04,642 --> 00:03:08,771
Maybe you already know her.
You just don't notice.

78
00:03:12,108 --> 00:03:13,234
Come on, let's eat.

79
00:03:13,776 --> 00:03:15,778
My treat, so you'll cheer up.

80
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:17,822
Honestly,

81
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:20,950
I'm so happy because…

82
00:03:23,328 --> 00:03:24,871
we're a couple now! [laughs]

83
00:03:24,954 --> 00:03:26,873
What? You thought I got rejected?

84
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:29,292
This wouldn't have happened without you.

85
00:03:30,585 --> 00:03:32,712
Seriously? You're really together?

86
00:03:32,795 --> 00:03:33,880
Yes! [chuckles softly]

87
00:03:34,547 --> 00:03:36,299
Isn't it too soon?

88
00:03:37,133 --> 00:03:38,885
Just one date and you're already a couple?

89
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:41,971
Cathy decided not to delay it anymore.

90
00:03:42,055 --> 00:03:43,097
I didn't expect it either.

91
00:03:43,181 --> 00:03:46,434
[in English] But I'm happy,
and it works for us.

92
00:03:47,018 --> 00:03:50,730
But you don't really know each other yet,

93
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:52,232
and she already said yes.

94
00:03:53,441 --> 00:03:55,735
Sorry, Gav, but isn't that a red flag?

95
00:03:56,861 --> 00:03:58,529
Come on, Karla.

96
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:01,157
Even if she's my girlfriend now,

97
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:03,368
of course we'll still get
to know each other,

98
00:04:03,451 --> 00:04:06,162
and if she doesn't like
something about me,

99
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:07,247
we can work it out.

100
00:04:08,539 --> 00:04:15,296
♪ <i>Don't get ahead</i> ♪

101
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:18,549
♪ <i>Of what the heart feels…</i> ♪

102
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:19,759
Gavsy!

103
00:04:19,842 --> 00:04:21,761
[in English] Babe, you came!

104
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:26,057
Uh, can you take a video
of me while I donate blood?

105
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:28,476
[in English] So, I can post it
on my socials for awareness.

106
00:04:28,559 --> 00:04:29,519
Sure, let's go.

107
00:04:29,602 --> 00:04:31,479
[in English] Perfect.
Thank you so much! Let's go!

108
00:04:32,272 --> 00:04:33,564
♪ <i>In every game…</i> ♪

109
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:34,899
"Gavsy"?

110
00:04:35,775 --> 00:04:36,776
[in English] "Babe"?

111
00:04:37,986 --> 00:04:38,903
Gross.

112
00:04:38,987 --> 00:04:43,366
♪ <i>Not that</i> ♪

113
00:04:43,449 --> 00:04:47,704
♪ <i>I'm thinking badly</i> ♪

114
00:04:47,787 --> 00:04:48,871
♪ <i>There are many like you…</i> ♪

115
00:04:48,955 --> 00:04:49,789
Hmm.

116
00:04:50,623 --> 00:04:51,874
[slurps] That's it.

117
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:53,001
[clicks tongue] Hit the spot.

118
00:04:54,335 --> 00:04:55,211
Exactly.

119
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:58,256
Here, Netchai.

120
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:02,802
[line rings]

121
00:05:02,885 --> 00:05:04,470
Hello, Tonet.

122
00:05:05,054 --> 00:05:06,681
Oh, just reminding you.

123
00:05:06,764 --> 00:05:10,852
We're eating later at that
roast pig restaurant I found at the mall.

124
00:05:10,935 --> 00:05:13,438
Twelve-thirty, okay? I reserved a table.

125
00:05:13,521 --> 00:05:15,732
Okay, brother!

126
00:05:15,815 --> 00:05:18,359
Yes, yes. I'm on my way to the mall.

127
00:05:18,943 --> 00:05:19,944
I'm almost there.

128
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:22,238
Wait. What's the occasion?

129
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:23,489
[chuckles] Nothing.

130
00:05:23,573 --> 00:05:27,327
I just exceeded my order quota this month.

131
00:05:27,410 --> 00:05:30,830
So, I thought I'd treat you.

132
00:05:30,913 --> 00:05:33,124
Let's celebrate. Let's eat Lechon Cebu.

133
00:05:33,207 --> 00:05:34,042
Is that okay?

134
00:05:34,834 --> 00:05:38,004
Isn't your cholesterol high?

135
00:05:38,963 --> 00:05:41,507
We might end up at the morgue tomorrow.

136
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:42,467
[sneaky music playing]

137
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:44,802
[gasps, coughs]

138
00:05:44,886 --> 00:05:45,928
What's wrong with you?

139
00:05:46,512 --> 00:05:49,098
Eh-- What? You're exaggerating!

140
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:52,810
No, after eating lots of lechon,

141
00:05:52,894 --> 00:05:55,313
we'll walk home to digest what we ate.

142
00:05:55,396 --> 00:05:58,274
Then, if you want,
we'll chew all the grass we pass by.

143
00:05:58,357 --> 00:06:00,276
Would that work? Huh, would that work?

144
00:06:00,359 --> 00:06:01,986
But I just want to say, brother…

145
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:03,404
Congratulations to you.

146
00:06:03,488 --> 00:06:07,283
It seems you really succeeded
here in Manila.

147
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:09,660
It's like your life
is on another level now.

148
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:10,745
Ah, wow.

149
00:06:10,828 --> 00:06:12,330
Oh, fine, fine. Okay, okay, okay.

150
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:15,249
Don't forget, okay?

151
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:16,375
Twelve-thirty, okay?

152
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:18,336
Yes, yes!

153
00:06:18,419 --> 00:06:20,088
Love you, brother.

154
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:21,464
Bye. Take care.

155
00:06:22,048 --> 00:06:24,050
Yes, bye, brother. Bye-bye.

156
00:06:24,717 --> 00:06:25,551
[phone blips]

157
00:06:26,385 --> 00:06:27,261
Wait.

158
00:06:28,137 --> 00:06:29,347
That's Audrey's.

159
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:31,474
[suspicious music playing]

160
00:06:32,433 --> 00:06:33,601
Ah, sir!

161
00:06:33,684 --> 00:06:37,021
Can we follow that car? Thank you.

162
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:41,275
[tense music playing]

163
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:42,276
[softly] Thank you.

164
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:44,153
[Paldo] That's it, that's it.

165
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:45,905
[man] Kuya Kurt's pares
is really delicious.

166
00:06:45,988 --> 00:06:47,532
- [man] It's tasty.
- [Paldo] I'll take care of this, okay.

167
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:48,950
- Wow!
- I'll pay for all of this.

168
00:06:49,033 --> 00:06:50,910
- Wow!
- [men muttering]

169
00:06:50,993 --> 00:06:52,662
[lively chattering]

170
00:06:52,745 --> 00:06:53,579
- [man 1] Yes, I got this.
- [man 2] Rice, please.

171
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:54,872
I told you so.

172
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:56,207
Oh, rice. That's yours.

173
00:06:56,916 --> 00:06:57,959
- Do you want more?
- [man] So good.

174
00:06:58,042 --> 00:06:58,876
Nothing else?

175
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,503
- Just order.
- More rice, more rice.

176
00:07:00,586 --> 00:07:01,754
[man] Thanks, Boss Paldo.

177
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:03,047
- [man] Soft drinks.
- Brother Kurt…

178
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:03,965
[man] It's delicious.

179
00:07:04,799 --> 00:07:06,092
I thought, um…

180
00:07:06,175 --> 00:07:08,094
- your goddaughter, Denden,
- [Kurt] Hmm?

181
00:07:08,177 --> 00:07:10,346
- [sneaky music playing]
- will be the one selling here.

182
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:11,973
[in English] How come
she's not yet here?

183
00:07:12,056 --> 00:07:14,267
[in English] I've been,
you know, waiting for her.

184
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:16,144
- [chuckles softly]
- Yes.

185
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:18,312
I miss her like crazy, Brother Kurt!

186
00:07:18,896 --> 00:07:19,897
You guys are unbelievable.

187
00:07:19,981 --> 00:07:23,651
Actually, she's working on something
before coming here.

188
00:07:23,734 --> 00:07:24,861
But listen up.

189
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:27,363
Behave yourselves
when she sells here, okay?

190
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:28,531
- [man] Oh, you guys behave, huh.
- Huh, huh?

191
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:31,868
Do you have other goddaughters,
Brother Kurt?

192
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:34,120
- [coughs]
- We can't all go for Denden.

193
00:07:34,203 --> 00:07:35,705
Why are you even asking that?

194
00:07:35,788 --> 00:07:38,166
She'll only pick one among us, you know.

195
00:07:38,249 --> 00:07:40,168
- Who's the most handsome here?
- Me.

196
00:07:40,251 --> 00:07:41,961
Then, it's Brother Atoy!

197
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:43,504
You disagree?

198
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:44,964
[playful music playing]

199
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:47,508
Who's the second most handsome here?

200
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:50,261
Ah, c'mon! Tonet just rejected you.

201
00:07:50,344 --> 00:07:52,847
Actually, guys, speaking
of my goddaughter,

202
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:54,015
she's here now.

203
00:07:54,098 --> 00:07:55,975
[sneaky music playing]

204
00:07:56,058 --> 00:07:57,185
- [man 1] Wow!
- [man 2] Whoa!

205
00:07:57,268 --> 00:07:58,769
[Paldo] Oh, my goodness!

206
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:00,605
- [T-Bak] Wow!
- [Paldo] Move, move, move.

207
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:01,939
[man] Ooh-la-la!

208
00:08:02,023 --> 00:08:03,399
[Paldo] Hi, Denden. Hi, hi, hi.

209
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:05,234
- Hi, Godfather.
- [Kurt] How are you?

210
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:06,861
Is your head okay or still hurting?

211
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:08,779
- I'm fine now.
- [Kurt] Really?

212
00:08:08,863 --> 00:08:11,657
Where's the guy who caught the thief

213
00:08:11,741 --> 00:08:13,701
who stole my phone yesterday?

214
00:08:13,784 --> 00:08:15,077
Uh, um…

215
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:17,246
[Paldo] Uh… [clears throat]

216
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:18,456
Actually…

217
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:20,917
that was me.

218
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,919
I was the one who helped you.

219
00:08:23,878 --> 00:08:25,796
I just want to fix this barangay, so…

220
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:28,382
You know, I help people in need.

221
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,259
It wasn't you.

222
00:08:30,968 --> 00:08:32,845
He's also the one who elbowed my face.

223
00:08:33,846 --> 00:08:35,264
The handsome curly-haired guy.

224
00:08:35,932 --> 00:08:37,058
[man clears throat]

225
00:08:37,141 --> 00:08:38,184
It wasn't you.

226
00:08:38,267 --> 00:08:40,311
[sneaky music playing]

227
00:08:40,394 --> 00:08:41,229
Curly-haired?

228
00:08:44,398 --> 00:08:45,358
Handsome curly-haired guy?

229
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:48,152
[music fades]

230
00:08:50,738 --> 00:08:51,989
[in English] Sir Emerson.

231
00:08:53,866 --> 00:08:55,368
[in English] Have you seen Tonet?

232
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:59,664
[in English] Is it okay if I ask her out
on a date later?

233
00:09:00,831 --> 00:09:02,750
Hmm, mmm-mmm, mmm-mmm.

234
00:09:02,833 --> 00:09:04,335
No can do.

235
00:09:04,418 --> 00:09:07,755
[in English] You… don't, uh…

236
00:09:07,838 --> 00:09:09,507
ask later for a date.

237
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:13,344
[in English] Yes. She's, uh… make crazy,

238
00:09:13,427 --> 00:09:15,429
because, uh, we have a walk.

239
00:09:15,972 --> 00:09:17,932
[in English] Uh, I won't do that.

240
00:09:18,015 --> 00:09:19,392
[in English] I just want to ask her out.

241
00:09:20,601 --> 00:09:21,936
[in English] No. No, no, no.

242
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:25,314
[in English] You-- You don't…

243
00:09:26,357 --> 00:09:28,442
[in English] You… Uh--

244
00:09:28,526 --> 00:09:30,194
Not possible. It's hard.

245
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:33,739
Simply no, because we have plans.

246
00:09:33,823 --> 00:09:35,825
We have plans, so…

247
00:09:35,908 --> 00:09:39,912
[in English] You better date her to ask
in the next time.

248
00:09:39,996 --> 00:09:41,998
[in English] Uh, good luck. Better luck.

249
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:43,082
[in English] But…

250
00:09:43,165 --> 00:09:44,000
- [in English] No.
- [in English] I just--

251
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:45,001
[in English] No, no, no, no.

252
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:46,711
I mean, leave, leave.

253
00:09:46,794 --> 00:09:49,171
You go, hasta la vista. Okay?

254
00:09:50,214 --> 00:09:52,049
[in English] Okay, don't shy yourself.

255
00:09:52,133 --> 00:09:54,468
[in English] Okay,
good riddance. All right!

256
00:09:58,264 --> 00:10:00,600
Speaking English is really hard.

257
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:01,851
[quirkymusic playing]

258
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:03,644
You're really hard to talk to--

259
00:10:03,728 --> 00:10:04,895
Don't!

260
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:08,691
[music fades]

261
00:10:11,694 --> 00:10:13,487
[security] Ah, ma'am, ma'am, ma'am…

262
00:10:13,571 --> 00:10:14,488
What do you need?

263
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:17,283
[chuckles] Guard, I'm Tonet.

264
00:10:17,366 --> 00:10:19,702
I know Audrey Regalia.

265
00:10:19,785 --> 00:10:21,829
I just want to talk to her.

266
00:10:21,912 --> 00:10:23,289
It's important.

267
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:25,541
All right, follow me.

268
00:10:26,208 --> 00:10:27,376
[security guard] Let's go.

269
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:29,545
[tense music playing]

270
00:10:32,381 --> 00:10:34,425
[in English] Sorry, sorry, sorry, I--

271
00:10:34,508 --> 00:10:38,346
No, no, no, I don't-- [titters]
I don't cut up customers.

272
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:39,680
Uh, uh…

273
00:10:39,764 --> 00:10:41,641
W-What do you need done?

274
00:10:41,724 --> 00:10:44,727
[chuckles] Don't you remember me?

275
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:47,229
I'm the one you elbowed, then passed out.

276
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:49,690
I'm Brother Kurt's goddaughter.

277
00:10:50,483 --> 00:10:52,276
Ah, y-yes! [titters]

278
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,362
Yes, right? Yes, right?

279
00:10:54,445 --> 00:10:55,946
Well, sorry.

280
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:57,948
My apologies, I had--
I was talking to someone earlier,

281
00:10:58,032 --> 00:10:59,784
and I've got a lot on my mind.

282
00:10:59,867 --> 00:11:01,869
Uh, why… why are you here?

283
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:04,413
I just want to thank you.

284
00:11:04,955 --> 00:11:07,333
Here, I brought you my goods.

285
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:08,876
[chuckles]

286
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:11,879
Do you want to taste this…

287
00:11:12,463 --> 00:11:13,756
pineapple of mine? [chuckles]

288
00:11:14,298 --> 00:11:15,132
Uh--

289
00:11:20,137 --> 00:11:21,180
Mmm.

290
00:11:21,263 --> 00:11:23,516
[playful music playing]

291
00:11:23,599 --> 00:11:26,394
Delicious. Your pineapple is delicious.
[chuckles]

292
00:11:26,477 --> 00:11:28,437
Hey, let's taste the pineapple too!

293
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:29,647
Yes!

294
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:31,607
- [man 1] Share!
- [man 2] Yes.

295
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:33,025
[man] Let's go in there!

296
00:11:33,109 --> 00:11:37,029
[clamoring]

297
00:11:37,113 --> 00:11:38,030
[indistinct chattering]

298
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:39,115
[Emerson] All of you, leave.

299
00:11:39,198 --> 00:11:40,491
You're disturbing us!

300
00:11:41,158 --> 00:11:42,785
[clamoring]

301
00:11:42,868 --> 00:11:44,620
[indistinct chattering]

302
00:11:44,703 --> 00:11:45,788
[Paldo] Wait--

303
00:11:45,871 --> 00:11:46,914
Hold on.

304
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:50,334
[Emerson clears throat]

305
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:53,129
[chuckles] Sorry. Apologies.

306
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:55,005
You know, Emerson,

307
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:57,550
pineapple isn't the only thing
I'll let you taste.

308
00:11:58,384 --> 00:12:00,594
[stammering]

309
00:12:00,678 --> 00:12:02,763
[stuttering] O-okay, I'm okay
with your pineapple.

310
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:07,017
[giggles] What I mean is, other dishes.

311
00:12:07,768 --> 00:12:09,353
Do you want to have lunch together?

312
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:11,772
[quirky music playing]

313
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:14,233
What? Uh…

314
00:12:14,942 --> 00:12:16,485
It's just that…

315
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:19,572
No, I can't. I have…

316
00:12:19,655 --> 00:12:21,323
I have a date.

317
00:12:21,407 --> 00:12:22,700
[music fades]

318
00:12:23,284 --> 00:12:25,661
My-- My sister, Tonet.

319
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:27,913
Yes, because we have plans.

320
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:28,873
I'm taking her out.

321
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:30,624
[chuckles]

322
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:32,251
You're such a sweet brother.

323
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:34,587
You know, that's rare.

324
00:12:35,337 --> 00:12:37,548
Putting family first before flirting.

325
00:12:38,215 --> 00:12:39,550
Are we flirting?

326
00:12:39,633 --> 00:12:42,720
[giggling]

327
00:12:42,803 --> 00:12:43,888
No, no…

328
00:12:43,971 --> 00:12:47,016
What I mean is…

329
00:12:47,099 --> 00:12:51,604
My sister is my priority now.

330
00:12:51,687 --> 00:12:52,771
Yes, because…

331
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:54,815
We haven't seen each other
for a long time.

332
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:57,693
Now we're finally together.
I really want to make it up to her.

333
00:12:58,527 --> 00:12:59,987
Yes. [sighs]

334
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:02,781
Ah, ah-- And… [titters]

335
00:13:03,491 --> 00:13:06,160
Your pineapple is so sweet. Thank you.

336
00:13:06,243 --> 00:13:08,537
Do you want more? [chuckles]

337
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:11,207
[quirky music playing]

338
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:13,292
Oh, oh-- It's okay.

339
00:13:13,375 --> 00:13:15,461
Yes. I'll eat it later.

340
00:13:15,544 --> 00:13:16,462
Yes, I'll eat it later.

341
00:13:17,046 --> 00:13:18,380
Thank you.

342
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:20,508
Is Audrey here?

343
00:13:20,591 --> 00:13:23,636
Ah, Ma'am Audrey is in her room.
I'll just knock.

344
00:13:23,719 --> 00:13:25,221
What's your name again?

345
00:13:25,304 --> 00:13:26,847
Uh, Tonet.

346
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:28,307
- Okay, wait.
- Okay, okay.

347
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:30,351
[suspicious music playing]

348
00:13:30,434 --> 00:13:31,602
It's big.

349
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:40,861
[door lock clicks]

350
00:13:42,404 --> 00:13:43,614
- [Martina] Hi!
- [Tonet shrieks]

351
00:13:44,698 --> 00:13:46,325
[in English] I'm Martina.

352
00:13:46,408 --> 00:13:47,910
Audrey's sister-in-law.

353
00:13:47,993 --> 00:13:50,412
[in English] Sorry. Uh, how do you--
How do you know her?

354
00:13:50,496 --> 00:13:52,665
Uh, Audrey?

355
00:13:52,748 --> 00:13:56,669
I met her through Atoy, Janine's father.

356
00:13:56,752 --> 00:13:59,088
- Mmm.
- [Tonet] I work with Atoy.

357
00:13:59,171 --> 00:14:02,174
I didn't catch Audrey earlier.

358
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:05,511
But coincidentally, I saw
her car passing by.

359
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:06,554
So, I followed it.

360
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:08,430
[in English] Okay. Uh…

361
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:11,392
[in English] Must be a really
important matter for you to do that.

362
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:15,020
Yes, it's about their child.

363
00:14:16,021 --> 00:14:18,357
Why? Is there a problem with Janine?

364
00:14:19,775 --> 00:14:21,735
[in English] It's very personal.

365
00:14:21,819 --> 00:14:23,112
[in English] Family issue.

366
00:14:23,195 --> 00:14:24,530
- [dramatic sting]
- [sinister music playing]

367
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:26,031
[in English] Well, I'm-I'm family.

368
00:14:26,115 --> 00:14:28,659
She is my niece.
[in English] So, she's also my concern.

369
00:14:32,204 --> 00:14:35,457
Did Audrey have Janine DNA tested?

370
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:40,212
[in English] Are you saying that Janine
is not really their child?

371
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:45,634
Sorry, but maybe--

372
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:48,178
Who knows? Maybe the results
were wrong or…

373
00:14:48,262 --> 00:14:50,347
the specimen was tampered with.

374
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:53,601
Let's just retest to be sure.

375
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:57,938
[tense music playing]

376
00:14:58,022 --> 00:14:59,315
[in English] I think you should leave.

377
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:02,985
[music swells]

378
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:06,113
Oh, wait! Why are you telling me to leave?

379
00:15:06,196 --> 00:15:08,699
I didn't even come here for you.

380
00:15:08,782 --> 00:15:11,619
[in English] I'm not gonna let you talk
to Audrey and feed her with these

381
00:15:11,702 --> 00:15:14,413
wild theories about her daughter.

382
00:15:14,496 --> 00:15:17,750
She's already been through enough
emotional stress when she lost Janine.

383
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:20,252
[in English] And then, you're just going
to dismiss her child?

384
00:15:20,336 --> 00:15:21,962
I was the one who searched for that child,

385
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:24,423
so I know Janine
is really Audrey's daughter.

386
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:25,758
[sighs]

387
00:15:25,841 --> 00:15:28,886
All I want is for Audrey to be sure that…

388
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:31,055
Janine is truly her child.

389
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:33,807
Let's do another DNA test.

390
00:15:33,891 --> 00:15:38,354
Then let's check the blood.

391
00:15:38,437 --> 00:15:41,315
If it's correct, then we have no problem!

392
00:15:41,899 --> 00:15:43,233
At least we'll be certain.

393
00:15:43,817 --> 00:15:48,405
But what if Janine turns out
to be the wrong child?

394
00:15:49,114 --> 00:15:50,574
She doesn't need to do that,

395
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:52,451
and she doesn't need to listen to you.

396
00:15:52,534 --> 00:15:54,119
- [in English] Please, just leave.
- [dramatic sting]

397
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:56,455
Why don't you want me to talk to Audrey?

398
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:58,832
Are you hiding something?

399
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:02,002
[in English] Oh my God!
Just leave, please!

400
00:16:02,086 --> 00:16:03,671
I'm not leaving. I don't care.

401
00:16:03,754 --> 00:16:06,048
I'll talk to Audrey
whether you like it or not. Period.

402
00:16:06,131 --> 00:16:07,925
Audrey, Audrey!

403
00:16:08,008 --> 00:16:12,596
[tense music playing]

404
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:13,973
[knocks on door]

405
00:16:14,807 --> 00:16:15,808
Come in.

406
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:20,187
Ma'am, you have a visitor downstairs.

407
00:16:20,270 --> 00:16:21,438
She says her name is Tonet.

408
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:23,023
Tonet?

409
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:25,359
Uh, what does she want?

410
00:16:25,442 --> 00:16:28,570
She didn't say, but she wants
to talk to you.

411
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:32,992
All right. Please tell her
I'll just get dressed.

412
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:34,994
Okay. Ma'am, here's what you asked for.

413
00:16:35,619 --> 00:16:38,372
[music swells]

414
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:42,167
Where is Audrey anyway?

415
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:43,794
- This house is so big--
- [in English] Have you lost your mind?!

416
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:45,087
- Audrey!
- [in English] What are you doing?!

417
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:46,839
Leave me alone!

418
00:16:47,631 --> 00:16:50,759
Don't you want Audrey to know
that you found the wrong child?!

419
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:53,303
Because you wouldn't react like this if…

420
00:16:53,387 --> 00:16:54,680
you weren't hiding something.

421
00:16:55,723 --> 00:16:56,807
Or maybe

422
00:16:56,890 --> 00:16:59,226
you already know
Janine isn't really their child,

423
00:16:59,309 --> 00:17:00,352
and you just don't want to be exposed?

424
00:17:00,436 --> 00:17:02,771
Shut up! Leave now! Get out of my house.

425
00:17:02,855 --> 00:17:04,398
- [in English] Get out of my house!
- Audrey!

426
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:07,109
[in English] Leave my house!

427
00:17:07,192 --> 00:17:09,194
Why are you pushing my wife, huh?
What's your problem? Who are you?!

428
00:17:09,278 --> 00:17:10,362
You're a trespasser, aren't you?

429
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:13,323
- Do you want me to kill you?!
- Whoa, whoa!

430
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:14,700
You don't need to threaten me.

431
00:17:14,783 --> 00:17:16,577
Yes, I'll leave.

432
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:18,078
I'll leave.

433
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:21,749
[in Visayan] It looks like
you're up to no good.

434
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:24,710
[in Visayan] Doesn't matter.

435
00:17:24,793 --> 00:17:25,961
[in Visayan] The truth
will eventually come out.

436
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:28,756
What did you say? Huh?

437
00:17:28,839 --> 00:17:31,967
Ah, I said… you're handsome!

438
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:34,636
I have something to do, so I'll go now.

439
00:17:35,679 --> 00:17:37,723
- Your haircut looks great…
- Leave!

440
00:17:42,853 --> 00:17:45,230
You need to follow that woman.

441
00:17:45,314 --> 00:17:46,774
She suspects something about Janine.

442
00:17:46,857 --> 00:17:48,650
That's why she wants to talk to Audrey.

443
00:17:48,734 --> 00:17:50,402
How did she find out?

444
00:17:50,486 --> 00:17:51,862
I don't know!

445
00:17:51,945 --> 00:17:54,907
[in English] But we can only stop her
from seeing Audrey now!

446
00:17:54,990 --> 00:17:56,116
[in English] She works for Atoy.

447
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,868
Anytime, she could tell Audrey.

448
00:17:57,951 --> 00:17:59,203
[in English] She's a ticking time bomb.

449
00:17:59,286 --> 00:18:00,621
We can't be exposed.

450
00:18:10,798 --> 00:18:12,424
[music fades]

451
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:16,678
[muffled chattering]

452
00:18:16,762 --> 00:18:17,888
Oh, Ibyang, what about you?

453
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:19,264
Do you want to buy something?

454
00:18:20,265 --> 00:18:21,391
I'm fine.

455
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:23,393
That's good.

456
00:18:27,064 --> 00:18:28,899
Daddy, it's so cute!

457
00:18:28,982 --> 00:18:30,984
I want that. Buy it for me! Please!

458
00:18:32,694 --> 00:18:33,904
[Ibyang] Janine!

459
00:18:34,613 --> 00:18:37,282
You've already asked Tatoy
to buy so many things!

460
00:18:37,366 --> 00:18:40,077
He might go broke because of you!

461
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,912
[scoffs] So what?

462
00:18:42,454 --> 00:18:44,540
Why are you meddling, huh?

463
00:18:45,457 --> 00:18:47,084
Ah, I know.

464
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:49,503
You're jealous.

465
00:18:49,586 --> 00:18:51,213
Daddy can afford it.

466
00:18:51,296 --> 00:18:52,464
He has lots of money.

467
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:55,259
[sneaky music playing]

468
00:18:55,342 --> 00:18:58,428
Ah, Janine, my dear.

469
00:18:58,512 --> 00:19:00,597
Just because we have money

470
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:04,852
and can spend doesn't mean
we should buy everything.

471
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:07,354
We should only get what we need, okay?

472
00:19:07,437 --> 00:19:09,148
Hmm? Okay?

473
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:10,274
[in English] Okay, Daddy.

474
00:19:14,069 --> 00:19:15,571
You little pest.

475
00:19:17,072 --> 00:19:18,407
I have an idea.

476
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:20,325
Why don't we just watch a movie instead?

477
00:19:20,409 --> 00:19:22,703
<i>Wonderkids</i> is showing now. I saw it.

478
00:19:22,786 --> 00:19:23,704
What do you think?

479
00:19:23,787 --> 00:19:24,955
G! I want that!

480
00:19:25,038 --> 00:19:27,082
- Actually, I like it more.
- Come on, let's buy tickets.

481
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:28,375
We don't have tickets yet!

482
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:30,752
Looks like it's starting in…

483
00:19:31,712 --> 00:19:33,672
ten minutes. Come on, let's buy tickets.

484
00:19:33,755 --> 00:19:37,259
[bright music playing]

485
00:19:37,342 --> 00:19:38,510
[Atoy] Come on, come on, come on.

486
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:43,515
Nanny, where's Tonet?

487
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:46,185
She already left, ma'am.

488
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:48,520
She was talking to Ma'am Martina earlier.

489
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:50,480
- What?
- [suspicious music playing]

490
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:53,609
- Martina, did you talk to Tonet?
- [footsteps approaching]

491
00:19:53,692 --> 00:19:55,110
[Martina, in English] Um, yes.

492
00:19:55,694 --> 00:19:57,404
[in English] Small talk, no-nothing much.

493
00:19:58,197 --> 00:19:59,573
Why did she leave?

494
00:19:59,656 --> 00:20:01,825
We didn't even meet.

495
00:20:01,909 --> 00:20:04,369
I don't know.
She didn't leave any message.

496
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:06,205
She just suddenly left.

497
00:20:06,288 --> 00:20:08,540
[in English] Um, anyway, I got to go!

498
00:20:10,292 --> 00:20:12,002
- [music fades]
- [door clicks open and shut]

499
00:20:13,003 --> 00:20:15,672
[tense music playing]

500
00:20:27,184 --> 00:20:28,185
- [man 1] Come back here!
- [man 2] Bro!

501
00:20:28,268 --> 00:20:29,394
- [clamoring]
- [man 2] What?! Huh?!

502
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:31,521
- I'll pay, bro!
- Pay what, huh?!

503
00:20:31,605 --> 00:20:32,898
I'll return your money!

504
00:20:32,981 --> 00:20:34,149
You're so hard to order around!

505
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:35,484
You're nosy!

506
00:20:36,026 --> 00:20:38,445
[grunting]

507
00:20:38,528 --> 00:20:40,364
[screaming]

508
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:46,995
[gasping]

509
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:48,789
[man 1] I'll chase you!

510
00:20:48,872 --> 00:20:50,207
Jesus.

511
00:20:50,290 --> 00:20:52,084
My lineage almost got cut off!

512
00:20:52,167 --> 00:20:53,794
[ominous music playing]

513
00:20:53,877 --> 00:20:55,504
- [horn blaring]
- [gasps]

514
00:20:55,587 --> 00:20:57,005
Damn you!

515
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:59,591
[dramatic sting]

516
00:20:59,675 --> 00:21:00,509
Damn.

517
00:21:01,969 --> 00:21:02,803
So hard-- [shrieks]

518
00:21:02,886 --> 00:21:04,429
- [anxious music playing]
- [gasping]

519
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:06,932
Ma'am, please don't treat me like that.

520
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:12,229
Already escaped death twice.

521
00:21:13,063 --> 00:21:15,315
But on the third…

522
00:21:16,191 --> 00:21:17,025
it will be final.

523
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:20,237
Is that a riddle or…

524
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:21,863
are you rap battling me?

525
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:23,615
[old woman] Listen.

526
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:29,246
The misfortune you suffered
is counted as three.

527
00:21:30,455 --> 00:21:31,790
If not you,

528
00:21:32,416 --> 00:21:33,458
then maybe…

529
00:21:34,167 --> 00:21:36,920
the one you love.

530
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:39,339
[music swells]

531
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,428
[music fades]

532
00:21:44,511 --> 00:21:46,013
[clears throat] Uh…

533
00:21:46,096 --> 00:21:47,931
[titters] Um…

534
00:21:48,015 --> 00:21:49,474
Oh, no, ah…

535
00:21:49,558 --> 00:21:52,644
Ma'am, no. Um, here, take all of this.

536
00:21:52,728 --> 00:21:54,396
Ma'am, maybe you haven't had lunch yet.

537
00:21:54,479 --> 00:21:56,064
You're just hungry.

538
00:21:56,148 --> 00:21:58,275
Better eat first.

539
00:21:58,358 --> 00:22:01,111
Because sometimes hungry people
turn into poetic fortune tellers.

540
00:22:01,194 --> 00:22:03,196
There's good porridge over there.

541
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:05,699
At Dexter's place. Just tell them.

542
00:22:05,782 --> 00:22:07,534
[anxious music playing]

543
00:22:19,463 --> 00:22:20,297
‪[Tonet gasping]

544
00:22:22,215 --> 00:22:23,592
[music fades]

545
00:22:26,428 --> 00:22:28,388
Make your men follow that woman.

546
00:22:29,222 --> 00:22:30,974
Don't let her get close to Atoy.

547
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:32,851
[suspicious music playing]

548
00:22:32,934 --> 00:22:33,810
[Tonet] Let's go, sir.

549
00:22:33,894 --> 00:22:35,353
[car engine starts]

550
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:41,026
We'll follow you. Update me.

551
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:43,737
What's our plan for her, boss?

552
00:22:45,614 --> 00:22:46,907
We'll profit from her.

553
00:22:48,533 --> 00:22:49,493
If she resists…

554
00:22:50,744 --> 00:22:51,661
you know what to do.

555
00:22:51,745 --> 00:22:54,247
[music swells]

556
00:22:58,585 --> 00:23:01,713
Roger, we'll take action.

557
00:23:07,761 --> 00:23:10,055
[motorcycle engine starts]

558
00:23:14,893 --> 00:23:19,856
- [electronic blipping]
- [tense music playing]

559
00:23:25,153 --> 00:23:26,279
- Oh, Atoy-- Ouch-
- [man] Hey!

560
00:23:26,363 --> 00:23:27,531
[Emerson] Hey!

561
00:23:27,614 --> 00:23:28,990
[Emerson] What the-- Hey.

562
00:23:29,074 --> 00:23:30,200
Stop! He's a thief!

563
00:23:30,283 --> 00:23:31,326
[Emerson] <i>Wait, my wallet?</i>

564
00:23:31,409 --> 00:23:32,577
‪UP NEXT

565
00:23:35,413 --> 00:23:36,248
- Hey.
- Stop!

566
00:23:42,212 --> 00:23:43,880
Atoy!

567
00:23:43,964 --> 00:23:45,257
Where are you going?

568
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:46,675
You followed me?

569
00:23:46,758 --> 00:23:47,968
[Red] Yes.

570
00:23:49,094 --> 00:23:50,387
So come with me…

571
00:23:51,555 --> 00:23:53,140
unless you want me
to put a hole in your side.

572
00:23:53,890 --> 00:23:55,350
[Atoy] <i>You really made me chase you.</i>

573
00:23:55,433 --> 00:23:57,018
Give me back my friend's wallet.

574
00:23:57,102 --> 00:23:58,436
Keep the money.

575
00:23:58,520 --> 00:24:00,230
The voucher. I need the voucher.

576
00:24:00,313 --> 00:24:01,731
It's important to him.
Give me the voucher.

577
00:24:01,815 --> 00:24:02,774
This?

578
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:04,776
I won't give it
without something in return.

579
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:07,779
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

580
00:24:10,907 --> 00:24:12,159
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

581
00:24:12,242 --> 00:24:14,703
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

582
00:24:14,786 --> 00:24:17,998
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

583
00:24:18,081 --> 00:24:19,249
‪♪ <i>‪Fix it</i>‪ ♪

584
00:24:19,332 --> 00:24:21,543
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
